@@ -737,0 +738,18 @@ survives exactly the sanity checks people run.
+- **Dawn in Node (`npm install webgpu`) validates *and runs* WGSL in the cloud container, on lavapipe.**
+  With no driver it finds no adapter. `apt-get install -y mesa-vulkan-drivers`, then
+  `VK_ICD_FILENAMES=/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.json` gives `mesa/software/llvmpipe` with
+  timestamp-query, subgroups (size 8) and shader-f16. In the Cowork cloud container, queue submissions
+  complete, so you can read results back and check them numerically. The claude.ai container
+  compiles but never completes a submission. 910 kernels compiled in 17 s and 656 configs verified in
+  40 s on 2 cores. (`refractometer/run/check.mjs`)
+- **Dawn in Node: keep a reference to the object `create([])` returns.** `openDevice(create([]))` lets the
+  `GPU` instance be garbage-collected. After any pause (a 3 s sleep, a busy loop), the next pipeline
+  creation aborts the whole process with `std::system_error: Invalid argument` or "The futex facility
+  returned an unexpected error code". It looks like a sandbox or threading fault and is not one.
+  Store the instance next to the device. (`refractometer/web/refract.js` `openDevice`)
+- **Verify a kernel before timing it, and test the check with mutants that change values.** A
+  sweep that times configs without checking them can crown a fast wrong kernel. Integer-valued test data
+  (0–6) makes f32 reductions exact in any order, so the comparison can use tolerance 0. Matmul data in
+  multiples of 1/8 is exact in f16 and in f32 sums at K=512. When testing the gate, a mutant that only
+  permutes a reduction's indices still passes, because sums ignore order; poison a value instead.
+  (`refractometer/run/check.mjs`, 48/48 mutants rejected)
